#
# Conformance case: contracts/probabilistic-stable-model-unsupported
# AC: a ReasoningContract that pairs a probabilistic uncertainty
# measure (logic:ProbabilisticMeasure) with stable-model semantics
# (logic:StableModelSemantics) is a FORBIDDEN facet combination
# (RuleNoProbabilisticStableModel): a calibrated probability mass is not
# well-defined over the multiple incomparable answer sets stable-model semantics
# admits. The compile MUST emit an UNSUPPORTED_CONTRACT Severity::Error and the
# harness MUST short-circuit before evaluating — the "unsupported is a hard stop"
# guarantee, pinned at the corpus level (profile.json declares
# "expect_unsupported": true).
#
# A logic:ProbabilityModel is declared so the ONLY unsupported reason is the
# probabilistic/stable-model conflict (not the graph-dependent
# RuleProbabilisticRequiresModel), keeping the case precisely about the intended
# forbidden combination.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/contracts/probabilistic-stable-model/> .

ex:UnsupportedContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:modelSemantics logic:StableModelSemantics ;
    logic:uncertaintyMeasure logic:ProbabilisticMeasure .

# Declare a probability model so the lone unsupported reason is the forbidden
# probabilistic + stable-model pairing.
ex:probModel a logic:ProbabilityModel .
